<title>UK: Tanker leaks oil off South Korea.</title>
<headline>Tanker leaks oil off South Korea.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A tanker carrying over two million tonnes of crude oil underwent temporary repairs in South Korea after some of the cargo leaked from a cracked tank and spread 15 miles to the northeast, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 315,000 dwt Berge Borg leaked the oil last Friday after sustaining two five millimetre cracks in the hull while unloading its cargo at Ulsan, Lloyds said, and added: &quot;The clean-up operation was nearly completed on December 15.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;The vessel is under investigation by the authorities and will be sailing soonest.</p>
<p>No more details were immediately available.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
